00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.534
I'm going to show you five
different tweets, and we're all

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.634
gonna vote on whether
you like each one or not.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.934
You all have voting clickers
at your seats?

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.534
Yep.
Look at the confusion there.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.133
There you go. Perfect.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.767
You can vote for all of
these tweets, by the way,

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.234
if you like them. We'll see.

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.067
You'll see the voting polls
when they come in.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.434
You can vote for none of them

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.033
if you feel like
voting for none of them,

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.767
if you go like, "I don't even
want to play this, Jimmy.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.601
Just do the work
and just leave me alone."

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:43.367
I understand. You're gonna
see the results live.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.033
Higgins, Roots,
you have clickers, too.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.200
-Got 'em.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.767
-Now, have you ever
gotten close on this?

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.334
Like, have you chosen
the right one?

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:50.734
-Yeah.
I always choose the right one.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.934
I've never gotten it wrong.

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:55.567
Have a perfect score
so far on "WeTweet."

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.167
-Alright. Let me see.
Here you go.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.501
So, anyways, we're gonna vote.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.067
Whichever one you like,
we're gonna tweet it out.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:04.701
And then you at home
can like it and WeTweet it.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.000
-Hm!
-It's a shared experience.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.234
Thank you very much.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.267
